cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use PanelHLA, please cite the software and the accompanying paper.
title: PanelHLA
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Nextflow DSL2 workflow that runs modality-appropriate HLA class-I
  callers, harmonises their outputs to canonical two-field allele pairs, and records
  the evidence behind every integration decision. The primary method is unweighted
  plurality over a modality-appropriate caller panel.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/uoozcan/PanelHLA"
url: "https://github.com/uoozcan/PanelHLA"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "TO CONFIRM - set at the tagged release"
keywords:
  - HLA typing
  - consensus methods
  - ensemble benchmarking
  - immunogenomics
  - reproducible workflows
  - exome sequencing
  - RNA sequencing
